From f97ff0bdcd729ce4ec01ba9a8508eabf0c41b2ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:30:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] SystemUI: cache the colored status bar icons setting

NotificationIconContainer read Settings.System.STATUSBAR_COLORED_ICONS
for every icon each time it applied or reset the icon states, and
IconManager and StatusBarIconView read it again for every icon they
created or updated. The reads pass USER_CURRENT, which skips the
SettingsProvider client cache, so each one was a binder call on the
main thread: a perfetto trace showed 16 'settings' binder calls per
NotificationStackScrollLayout#updateChildren, taking 2229 of its
3141 ms.

Read the setting once into StatusBarIconView, keep it current from a
ContentObserver for all users and on user switch, and have every call
site use that value. IconManager's observer re-reads it before it
refreshes the icons, as it can run before the cache's own observer,
so the colored icons toggle still applies right away.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
